<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huey Tlatoani</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Great Speaker</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huey Tlatoani, meaning Great Speaker, was the title of the supreme ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> and the Aztec Triple Alliance. The holder was chosen from the royal lineage by a council of nobles. He combined military, political and religious leadership in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huey-tlatoani.jpg" alt="Huey Tlatoani" width="295" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nezahualpiltzintli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
